  "supervision": {
    "boundary_char": ",",
    "field": "subject_type",
    "learn_chars": "each row's target is written whole and only its head — through the subject_type value AND the one separator character that closes it — is supervised. `scripts/train_qlora.py` masks the rest out of the loss. The separator is inside the boundary because the mask is applied on token END offsets: with the boundary ON the value, a tokenizer that merges the closing quote with the comma produces a token ending one character past it, and that whole merge — the value's tail with it — falls out of supervision. It teaches structure the parser demands and no label; the two unlabelled fields are as untaught as they were",
    "unsupervised_fields": [
      "subject_id",
      "stance"
    ],
    "why": "the team lead labelled subject_type and nothing else. Training the two unlabelled fields as null would teach «stance is always null», and three of the fourteen sealed gold rows score stance — the reachable maximum would fall to 11 against a threshold of 12 and the gate would be unreachable by construction"
